  "goodToKnow": "Der Mathematiker (die Mathematikerin) is a mathematician. Germany produced many famous ones: Carl Friedrich Gauss (on the old 10 DM note), Leibniz, Riemann, Hilbert and Emmy Noether, a pioneer of abstract algebra. In schools, Mathematik is shortened to Mathe. Many mathematicians work in insurance as actuaries (Aktuare) or in IT. Plural: die Mathematiker."
